moxie-cores licensing
=====================

Unless a file says otherwise, moxie-cores is

    Copyright (c) Anthony Green <green@moxielogic.com>

and is free software, distributed under the terms of the GNU General
Public License version 2 as published by the Free Software
Foundation (GPL-2.0-only).  The license is in COPYING.

Some files say otherwise.  They keep their own licenses, as their
headers or the files beside them state; these are the ones that do:

  cores/hex_display/hex_display.v, cores/hex_display/seg_7.v
      From the Zet processor, by Zeus Gomez Marmolejo: GNU GPL
      version 3 or later (COPYING3).

  cores/uart3/uart.v
      Ultra-Embedded.com: GNU LGPL version 2.1 or later.

  cores/statled
      From OpenCores: GNU LGPL version 2.1 or later.

  cores/altera_sdram
      MIT license.

  cores/LVT-regs
      Charles Eric LaForest's example code: "Permission is granted for
      any use, and attribution would be nice."  See its README.txt.

  firmware/bootrom/handler.S, firmware/bootrom/tinystub.c
      Anthony Green: two-clause BSD license.

  scripts/microcoder.lisp, scripts/msgmaker.lisp,
  cores/moxibit/ucoder.lisp, bench/mox125/test.lisp,
  bench/mox125/zephyr.lisp, bench/icache/test.lisp
      Anthony Green: GNU GPL version 3 or later (COPYING3).

The FuseSoC core files say the same in their license fields.
